# INTRO
introSlug: outdoor-kitchens
intro:
  heading: "Turnkey Outdoor Kitchens Built for New England Entertaining"
  paragraphs:
    - >
      Bring the comfort and culinary capabilities of your indoor kitchen outdoors. S. Phaneuf & Associates designs and builds custom outdoor kitchens throughout Massachusetts, transforming backyards in Concord, Holliston, Wellesley, and across MetroWest into luxury outdoor entertainment destinations. From streamlined grilling islands to expansive L-shaped outdoor chef suites with wood-fired pizza ovens and cocktail bars, we create spaces built around your entertaining lifestyle.
    - >
      Outdoor kitchens in Massachusetts face severe environmental stresses: blistering summer heat, driving fall rains, and sub-zero winter freeze-thaw cycles. We never build temporary wood-framed islands that rot or warp. Every outdoor kitchen we construct features a reinforced concrete frost footing poured 48 inches below grade, a solid concrete masonry unit (CMU) core, and hand-selected natural stone veneer cladding.
    - >
      We coordinate the entire build—from initial architectural drawings and footing excavation to utility rough-ins (gas, electric, plumbing), granite fabrication, and appliance installation—providing a smooth, single-contract construction experience.

# 1. PAGE OPTIONS (SPECIFIC TO OUTDOOR KITCHENS)
pageOptions:
  heading: "Custom Outdoor Kitchen Features & Configurations"
  intro: >
    We customize every outdoor kitchen island around your preferred cooking appliances, layout geometry, and stone finishes.
  items:
    - title: "Built-In Stainless Steel Grilling Islands"
      description: >
        The centerpiece of any outdoor kitchen. We build custom grill enclosures tailored for high-performance 32" to 54" built-in natural gas and propane grills (Lynx, Blaze, Wolf, Kalamazoo). Enclosures include vented cutouts, access doors, pull-out trash drawers, and warming cabinets sheathed in natural New England fieldstone or ledgestone veneer.
      features:
        heading: "Grilling Island Highlights"
        items:
          - "Engineered non-combustible CMU construction with stainless heat shields"
          - "Internal gas shutoff coordination and integrated low-voltage lighting"
          - "Integrated storage drawers, access doors, and double trash roll-outs"
          - "Seamlessly integrated into bluestone or paver patio surrounds"

    - title: "Outdoor Dining Bars & Beverage Stations"
      description: >
        Enhance your outdoor hosting with elevated bar-height seating counters, built-in outdoor under-counter refrigerators, outdoor ice makers, and stainless steel beverage tubs. We build footrests with granite treads and integrate GFCI electrical outlets for blender stations and smart entertainment systems.
      features:
        heading: "Bar & Beverage Highlights"
        items:
          - "Comfortable 42-inch bar height with 12-inch countertop overhangs"
          - "Weatherproof marine-grade outdoor refrigeration enclosures"
          - "Integrated under-counter LED strip lighting for nighttime ambiance"
          - "Durable polished granite or leathered quartzite service tops"

    - title: "Wood-Fired & Gas Outdoor Pizza Ovens"
      description: >
        Authentic artisanal pizza ovens bring gourmet dining and theatrical cooking to your patio. We construct heavy-duty stone masonry pizza oven enclosures using refractory firebrick, specialized high-temp mortar, and authentic fieldstone cladding with integrated wood storage cubbies underneath.
      features:
        heading: "Pizza Oven Highlights"
        items:
          - "Refractory firebrick hearths capable of sustaining 900°F cooking heat"
          - "Built-in dry firewood storage niches framed with stone lintels"
          - "Stainless steel or masonry flue chimneys positioned for proper draft"
          - "Available in traditional wood-burning or hybrid gas-assist configurations"

    - title: "Outdoor Prep Counters & Sink Stations"
      description: >
        A fully functional outdoor kitchen requires ample food prep space. We install deep stainless sinks, pull-out faucets, and continuous granite countertops that give you prep surfaces right beside the grill, so you never have to run back and forth inside the house.
      features:
        heading: "Prep Station Highlights"
        items:
          - "Seamless integration of deep undermount stainless outdoor sinks"
          - "Trash chute cutouts and integrated cutting board counters"
          - "Dedicated plumbing winterization drain valves for easy end-of-season shutoff"
          - "Stain-resistant sealed granite prep areas"

# 2. TECHNICAL SPECS (SPECIFIC TO OUTDOOR KITCHENS)
technicalSpecs:
  heading: "Engineered Construction & Utility Standards"
  intro: >
    Outdoor kitchens require rigorous structural and utility engineering to ensure safety, fire prevention, and frost stability.
  items:
    - title: "Frost-Depth Reinforced Concrete Foundation Slab"
      description: >
        An outdoor kitchen cannot be placed directly on sand or pavers. We excavate 48 inches below finished grade to pour structural concrete footings or a reinforced 8-inch concrete slab with #4 rebar grid, eliminating settlement cracks.
    - title: "Concrete Block (CMU) Structural Substructure"
      description: >
        We construct the island core using industrial concrete masonry units (cinder blocks) bound with structural mortar. This provides an immovable, rot-proof, 100% non-combustible housing for high-temperature grills.
    - title: "Natural Stone Veneer & Mortar Scratch Coat"
      description: >
        The block exterior is covered with galvanized metal lath, a polymer-modified scratch coat, and hand-chiseled natural thin stone veneer. Stone corners are wrapped with authentic L-shaped corner units for a monolithic look.
    - title: "Utility Trenching & Code Coordination"
      description: >
        We excavate dedicated trenches below frost depth for natural gas lines, 20-amp GFCI electrical conduits, and water lines, coordinating with licensed trades to guarantee 100% code compliance.

# 3. PAGE BENEFITS (SPECIFIC TO OUTDOOR KITCHENS)
pageBenefits:
  heading: "Why Choose S. Phaneuf for Your Outdoor Kitchen?"
  intro: >
    As master masons and heavy civil contractors, we deliver turnkey outdoor living suites that combine culinary performance with architectural beauty.
  items:
    - title: "Single-Source Turnkey Accountability"
      description: >
        From footing excavation and patio integration to stone veneer, countertop template, and appliance cutouts, we manage every phase under one contract.
    - title: "Built for All Four New England Seasons"
      description: >
        Non-combustible masonry and frost-proof footings ensure your outdoor kitchen weathers freezing snowstorms and blistering summer sun without deterioration.
    - title: "Natural Stone Artisanship"
      description: >
        Our master masons hand-dress native New England fieldstone, granite, and bluestone to complement your existing house architecture.
    - title: "Premium Resale Appeal"
      description: >
        A custom stone outdoor kitchen expands usable living square footage and is one of the highest-ROI luxury home improvements in Massachusetts.

# 4. PAGE PROCESS (SPECIFIC TO OUTDOOR KITCHENS)
pageProcess:
  heading: "Our 5-Step Outdoor Kitchen Build Process"
  intro: >
    From appliance selection to the first outdoor meal, our streamlined process ensures precision at every step.
  steps:
    - title: "1. Design Consultation & Appliance Selection"
      description: >
        We review your entertaining style, select appliance specifications (grill width, refrigerators, side burners), and establish island layout geometry.
    - title: "2. Trenching & Frost Footing Excavation"
      description: >
        We excavate below the 48-inch frost line, dig utility trenches for gas and power, and pour a heavy rebar-reinforced concrete footing slab.
    - title: "3. CMU Core Construction & Utility Rough-Ins"
      description: >
        Our masons lay the structural concrete block skeleton, rough in gas, water, and electrical conduits, and create custom stainless appliance framing.
    - title: "4. Stone Veneer Cladding & Granite Countertop Installation"
      description: >
        We apply the natural stone veneer facade and template, cut, and install custom polished granite or quartzite countertops with eased edges.
    - title: "5. Appliance Insertion, Testing & Final Handover"
      description: >
        We set stainless steel appliances, test gas fittings and electrical circuits, clean the entire work area, and deliver a fully operational kitchen.

# 5. PAGE FAQS (SPECIFIC TO OUTDOOR KITCHENS)
pageFaqs:
  heading: "Frequently Asked Questions About Outdoor Kitchens"
  items:
    - question: "How do you winterize an outdoor kitchen in Massachusetts?"
      answer: >
        Winterizing an outdoor kitchen is straightforward when built properly. Turn off water supply shutoff valves inside the house and blow out outdoor sink lines with compressed air to prevent burst pipes. Natural gas lines can remain active for winter grilling. We install 304/316 marine-grade stainless steel appliances that resist moisture and winter snow with custom vinyl covers.
    - question: "What countertop material is best for an outdoor kitchen in New England?"
      answer: >
        Natural granite with a flamed, honed, or leathered finish is the premier choice for Massachusetts outdoor kitchens. Unlike engineered quartz (which discolors and yellows under outdoor UV rays) or poured concrete (which is prone to hairline freeze-thaw cracks), dense natural granite handles extreme winter freezes, summer heat, and hot cookware without degrading.
    - question: "Do I need a building permit for an outdoor kitchen in Massachusetts?"
      answer: >
        Yes. Most Massachusetts municipalities require permits for structural footings, electrical branch circuits, and gas line extensions. S. Phaneuf & Associates coordinates all necessary documentation and works with licensed trade partners for safe, code-compliant utility connections.
    - question: "Can an outdoor kitchen be added onto an existing patio?"
      answer: >
        In most cases, an existing paver or stone patio cannot support the concentrated weight of a heavy masonry outdoor kitchen (which can weigh 4,000 to 10,000 lbs). We saw-cut the patio footprint, excavate down 48 inches below the regional frost line, and pour a reinforced concrete frost slab before building the stone structure.
    - question: "How long does it take to construct a custom outdoor kitchen?"
      answer: >
        A custom masonry outdoor kitchen typically takes 2 to 3 weeks of construction time, including footing excavation, block laying, utility rough-ins, stone veneer facing, and custom granite fabrication.

